## Decision Record

- Capability families, not files, are the unit of product architecture and disposition.
- One read-side project projection owns the shared interpretation of authority, planning,
  lifecycle, outcomes, reconciliation, closure, and bounded executive counts.
- Existing dashboard report fields remain stable; compatibility wrappers are allowed only while
  they delegate to the canonical builder and contain no interpretation logic.
- New feature proposals must state the existing surface they consume, replace, or retire and must
  report runtime-code delta. Unjustified parallel state models fail the reduction contract.
- The 100k presentation and operator loop are excluded from this roadmap; their Idea must consume
  this projection and consolidate existing overview/status/dashboard overlap.

## Recovery Contract

- Unknown or inconsistent authority continues to fail through the established resolver; the
  projection does not select or mutate authority.
- File and SQLite sources remain independently testable. A projection error cannot alter planning,
  lifecycle, outcome, relationship, or closure state.
- Wire-contract mismatch, privacy leakage, duplicate projection construction, failing focused
  checks, target mismatch, or stale exact-commit evidence leaves the campaign open at Work2.
- Broad command retirement and compatibility removal require separate usage evidence and explicit
  scope; they are not inferred from this consolidation candidate.

## Verification Strategy

- Contract tests for one projection envelope containing summary and exhaustive ledger.
- Existing authority, planning-order, campaign execution, and dashboard reporter tests rerouted
  through the shared seam, plus an explicit one-build-per-report regression.
- Source inventory and runtime-code delta report proving the candidate does not hide moved-line
  growth or a second project model.
- Strict Doctor and focused local suite, followed by exact-commit web, Linux, and Windows Work2
  deployment and checks through the repository orchestrator.
- Release-cohort registration against the governing campaign cycle and durable checkpoint/rebuild
  parity, with no push, publication, production deployment, or client synchronization.

## Authority Boundaries

This roadmap authorizes faithful planning, source and test changes, local commits, known
development deployment, focused qualification, release-cohort registration, and checkpointing at
Work2 under the current project preference. It does not authorize credentials, destructive
recovery, unknown targets, production delivery, a release, client synchronization, public command
removal, or implementation of IDEA-0028.

